course: dictionary
lesson: 9541
title: Stomp: feelings in a step
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To stomp means to walk with heavy, loud steps, often because you are angry. Read the words around it to be sure. «The Mouse stomps off insulted.» The word insulted tells you the Mouse is upset, so stomp shows its cross feelings.
explain: Stomp can also mean to stamp on something hard with your foot. «Foley artists stomp on gravel in a studio» means they stamp on the gravel to make a sound for a film, not that they are cross.
explain: Stomp can also be a noun: a heavy step, or a lively dance with heavy stamping steps. Check the clues. Is someone angry, or is the word about making a sound or keeping a beat?
fact: To stomp means to walk with heavy, loud steps.
fact: To stomp off means to walk away crossly, often because you are upset.
fact: To stomp on something means to stamp on it hard with your foot.
fact: A stomp is a heavy step, or a lively dance with heavy stamping steps.
fact: In sport slang, to stomp a team means to beat them easily.
exercise: «The Mouse stomps off insulted.» What does stomps off suggest? | Sings a long, sad song | Falls asleep on the spot | Dances happily around the room | *Walks away crossly with heavy steps
exercise: «Foley artists stomp on gravel in a studio.» What does stomp on mean here? | *Stamp hard on it with the foot | Smell it carefully | Sing a song about it | Sweep it into a neat pile
exercise: Which one best describes a stomp, the noun? | A type of small bird | A gentle whisper | *A heavy step or a lively dance with stamping | A long, quiet walk
test: «A rude Rhinoceros stomps up.» What does stomps up mean? | Climbs up a tree quickly | *Walks up with heavy, loud steps | Runs away in fear | Floats up quietly like a balloon
test: In sport slang, what does it mean to stomp a team? | To wait for them after the match | *To beat them easily | To stamp on their ball | To dance for them
exam: Jayden says «The Mouse stomps off» means the Mouse is happy. Why is he wrong? | Because stomp only means to sing | Because a mouse cannot walk | Because stomp means to dance happily | *Because stomping off shows the Mouse is cross and insulted
